<title>USA: J&amp;L Specialty Steel Q1 shr drops to $0.13.</title>
<headline>J&amp;L Specialty Steel Q1 shr drops to $0.13.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>							Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							    March 31,</p>
<p>							     1997	1996</p>
<p> Net sales					    $165,095 $184,926</p>
<p> Cost of products sold			     148,001  152,045</p>
<p> Depreciation and amortization expenses	  5,920    5,695</p>
<p>   Gross profit					 11,174   27,186</p>
<p> Selling, general and administrative expenses  5,001    4,846</p>
<p> Research and technology expense		   1,567    1,535</p>
<p> Unusual item					  (5,907)	---</p>
<p>   Operating income				   10,513   20,805</p>
<p> Interest income					  (35)    (158)</p>
<p> Interest expense					  715    1,213</p>
<p> Other (income) expense, net			  (41)	304</p>
<p>   Income before income taxes			9,874   19,446</p>
<p> Income taxes					    4,833    8,764</p>
<p>   Net income					    5,041   10,682</p>
<p>Per common share:</p>
<p>   Net income						.13	.28</p>
<p>   Dividends declared				    .10	.10</p>
<p> Tons shipped					   92,761   83,433</p>
<p>NOTE: Lower net sales and net income due primarily to lower sales prices, which were down 20 percent from the same period a year ago, according to company.</p>
<p>First quarter 1997 results include a one-time pretax gain of $5.9 million resulting from settlement of a commercial dispute with a third-party vendor.</p>
<p>Full company name is J&amp;L Specialty Steel Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
